          "image_source": "images/page_25_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.22,
            0.699,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "Are there other regular polygons that can tile the plane? What about equilateral triangles?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.346,
            0.261,
            0.652,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_25_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.394,
            0.846,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": "Tiling with equilateral triangles shows the possibility of tiling with another regular polygon."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.433,
            0.681,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": "A plane can be tiled using regular hexagons as well."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.357,
            0.453,
            0.643,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_25_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.605,
            0.848,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "A plane can also be tiled using more than one shape, and using non-regular polygons. People such as the great Dutch artist Escher (1898 – 1972) — whose works explored mathematical themes such as tiling — have come up with creative ways of tiling a plane with animal shapes! Here are some examples."
        },
        {
